cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below."
title: "asmsense-data: training and evaluation data for naming functions in stripped x86-64 binaries"
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: krxi
repository: "https://github.com/krxi/asmsense-data"
repository-code: "https://github.com/krxi/asmsense"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/krxi123/asmsense"
abstract: >-
  Chat-format training, validation and test data for asmsense. Inputs are
  anonymized x86-64 assembly (Mach-O, clang, -O0 to -Os), call context and, from
  v6, Ghidra decompilation; targets are the original function name plus
  one-sentence English and Turkish descriptions. The split is project-level and
  test projects are little-known and recent. Rows keep the licenses of the
  permissively licensed C projects they were compiled from.
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - binary analysis
  - function name recovery
  - stripped binaries
  - dataset
